#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ca4Ti3O10, Ruddlesden-Popper n = 3 calcium titanate, Pbca (No. 61), long axis c.
#
# Provenance (two sources, combined):
#  - Fractional coordinates: DFT-relaxed structure mp-15315 from the Materials Project
#    (https://materialsproject.org/materials/mp-15315, retrieved through the public OPTIMADE
#    endpoint https://optimade.materialsproject.org, CC BY 4.0), symmetrized with pymatgen.
#    The Materials Project entry is linked to the experimental ICSD entry 86242.
#  - Cell lengths: M. M. Elcombe, E. H. Kisi, K. D. Hawkins, T. J. White, P. Goodman and
#    S. Matheson, Acta Cryst. B47 (1991) 305-314, doi:10.1107/S0108768190013416, reported
#    in setting Pcab as a = 5.4083, b = 27.1432, c = 5.4337 A. Pcab is Pbca with a and b
#    exchanged, so in this Pbca setting a = 5.4083, b = 5.4337, c = 27.1432 A.
#    The DFT cell (5.4447, 5.5279, 27.1789 A) is replaced by these experimental lengths.
#
# No displacement parameters are given, so B is assumed by the reader.
# This structure is used only to generate hidden specimens; it is deliberately absent from
# the in-game reference library (a legitimate "missing reference" case).
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
